{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1764757,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"DataVerse","festival_id":520881,"organization_id":943045,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-22T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/dataverse-bharati-vidyapeeths-college-of-engineering-1764757","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>About the Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>DataVerse<\/strong> is a data-driven detective challenge where participating teams step into the shoes of investigators tackling a fictional case rooted in real-world Data-for-Earth problems. Across three progressive rounds, participants must spot misleading data, analyze complex datasets, deliver calibrated estimates, and defend their analytical conclusions before a panel of judges.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round Wise Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Spot the Lie<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: Offline, paper-based analytical investigation.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Teams are provided with a physical case file containing data points, visualizations, and claims. Without requiring prior Data Science knowledge, participants must critically analyze the material to uncover hidden flaws, misrepresentations, and misleading data points.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: The Data Room<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: Hands-on dataset investigation.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Shortlisted teams work directly with provided datasets and CSV files. Participants analyze the raw data, derive key insights, submit a numerical\/evidence-based estimate along with an assigned confidence level, and document their analytical methodology within the allotted time.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: The Defense<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: Live presentation &amp; cross-examination.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Finalist teams present their analysis and defend their methodology before the judging panel. Following the presentations, the <strong>Ground Truth<\/strong> is officially revealed.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to students from all B.Tech branches and academic years.<\/li>\n<li>Team Size: Teams must consist of <strong>2 to 3 members<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Data Integrity &amp; Fair Play:\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must rely strictly on the provided datasets and materials.<\/li>\n<li>Manipulation, misrepresentation, fabrication of evidence, or external unfair assistance is strictly prohibited and will lead to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Punctuality &amp; Submissions: All entries and analytical write-ups must be submitted within the specified time limits for each round.<\/li>\n<li>Evaluation Criteria:\n<ul>\n<li>Performance across all rounds contributes to final rankings.<\/li>\n<li>Key parameters include accuracy, evidence-based reasoning, soundness of analytical method, confidence calibration, data relevance, and clarity under defense.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Final Authority: The decision of the organizers and judging panel is final and non-contestable.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>For Queries Contact :-<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Riyanshu -&nbsp;<\/strong> 9318307237<\/p>\n<p><strong>Yuvraj Sapra -<\/strong> 9818964652<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33478161,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:11:59+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-02T17:39:24+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"xePrWkE","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":null,"display_title":